WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:03.300
Bellwether, recorded from the running product in paper mode on 27 September 2026. Prices are live; trades and burns are simulated.

2
00:00:03.350 --> 00:00:04.500
The landing page, with the engine running.

3
00:00:04.500 --> 00:00:07.900
The engine buys back and burns $ASH. The bell rings once and names the burn.

4
00:00:07.900 --> 00:00:10.520
Nothing rings unless the engine actually burned.

5
00:00:10.520 --> 00:00:13.450
The tape: every claim, trade and burn as it happens.

6
00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.300
Clicking a burn on the tape opens its receipt.

7
00:00:15.300 --> 00:00:18.600
Live: fees claimed, tokens bought back and burned, and trading equity, each with the time it was read.

8
00:00:18.600 --> 00:00:21.900
Open positions and the activity feed. Positions are pooled per market.

9
00:00:21.900 --> 00:00:25.650
Every registered token and the engine’s call on it. Opening Silicon Frog.

10
00:00:25.650 --> 00:00:27.850
Silicon Frog’s page: supply burned for good, and what the engine is doing right now.

11
00:00:27.850 --> 00:00:29.750
Launching a token: four steps.

12
00:00:29.750 --> 00:00:32.600
Step 1: choose a launchpad. Only one field on it differs from a normal launch.

13
00:00:32.600 --> 00:00:36.510
Pons is picked and joins the ticket on the right.

14
00:00:36.510 --> 00:00:39.900
Step 2: the stock the token’s trading book goes long on. NVDA is picked.

15
00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:41.990
The strategy stays Balanced. Continue.

16
00:00:41.990 --> 00:00:44.170
Step 3: the Bellwether wallet to paste as Pons’s Creator wallet.

17
00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.250
Copying the wallet address.

18
00:00:46.250 --> 00:00:50.990
On ponsfamily.com: the create form, then Advanced.

19
00:00:50.990 --> 00:00:52.900
Pasting the wallet into Creator wallet. Nothing is submitted or connected in this recording.

20
00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:54.550
Back on Bellwether: I’ve launched.

21
00:00:54.550 --> 00:00:57.640
Step 4: pasting the token’s contract address, a real token launched on Pons.

22
00:00:57.640 --> 00:01:00.400
All five on-chain checks pass, including that its creator fees go to the Bellwether wallet.

23
00:01:00.400 --> 00:01:03.300
What the engine will do for $FILL. Then: Ring the opening bell.

24
00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:06.100
$FILL is registered, and the bell rings once for it.

25
00:01:06.100 --> 00:01:09.800
Proof: what the engine’s ledger says it holds against what its wallets hold. The books balance.

26
00:01:09.800 --> 00:01:13.430
Launch a token at bellwether.fun. Always copy the wallet address from the launch page.
